         1 wells   drift vs the 1-well limit = 0.0000
        10 wells   drift vs the 1-well limit = 1.3715
        60 wells   drift vs the 1-well limit = 1.1334
       300 wells   drift vs the 1-well limit = 1.0536
      60 -> 300 wells changes the drift by 0.070
      (a drift that keeps growing with N is catalogue-row counting;
       one that converges is a genuine field with a coherence scale)
